(7134969, 1092068, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i> I do wish I could watch this process. There''s a chance that we might move to France for about 6 months in a year and a half or so. Can I sit and watch for a day, if I do? :)</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Wendy, much appreciated! I would imagine that watching me working on an image would be painfully boring, as it is often a slow process. However, it sure would be fun to meet, be sure to drop me a message when your trip is planned :)</td>', 'Originally posted by vawendy: I do wish I could watch this process. There''s a chance that we might move to France for about 6 months in a year and a half or so. Can I sit and watch for a day, if I do? :)  Thanks Wendy, much appreciated! I would imagine that watching me working on an image would be painfully boring, as it is often a slow process. However, it sure would be fun to meet, be sure to drop me a message when your trip is planned :)', '2013-11-26 01:30:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(7135050, 1092128, 144365, '<td valign="top">I was the baghead.<br/>Didn''t want people knowing I was back until the first challenge I entered was over. There''s a thread about my return, so I don''t care anymore.<br/> <br/>Forget the exact comment, but it was about my daughter also reading books. You were my only eight in the entire challenge.</td>', 'I was the baghead.Didn''t want people knowing I was back until the first challenge I entered was over. There''s a thread about my return, so I don''t care anymore. Forget the exact comment, but it was about my daughter also reading books. You were my only eight in the entire challenge.', '2013-11-26 08:45:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7135084, 1092128, 138630, '<td valign="top">Thanks to both of you and especially Chris for coming back and letting me know who had made the original comment - I was soooo curious :).  This was at the library - low artificial light and hand held, a situation my camera does not handle well in terms of noise.  Clifford is definitely muddy and I so wished I had the time and skills to change him out for a crisper version given the rule set, but I didn''t. Our granddaughter turned two the end of August, and she talks up a storm, not only to us but also to all her dolls and animals as you see here.  There were sweeter moments during the brief "shoot" but not with the book positioned well in terms of the Droste effect.</td>', 'Thanks to both of you and especially Chris for coming back and letting me know who had made the original comment - I was soooo curious :).  This was at the library - low artificial light and hand held, a situation my camera does not handle well in terms of noise.  Clifford is definitely muddy and I so wished I had the time and skills to change him out for a crisper version given the rule set, but I didn''t. Our granddaughter turned two the end of August, and she talks up a storm, not only to us but also to all her dolls and animals as you see here.  There were sweeter moments during the brief "shoot" but not with the book positioned well in terms of the Droste effect.', '2013-11-26 10:41:25.000000', NULL, 0),
